Space Waves Autoplayer
A screen-based bot for the browser game Space Waves. It watches your screen, detects the ship and obstacles, and plays automatically — no game files are read or modified.
What it does
Tracks the ship and plans a safe path around obstacles in real time
Detects moving hazards (gears) and predicts their motion
Recognizes and clicks common menu buttons (Give Up, Next, Retry, Continue Playing, No Thanks) using on-screen text — no guessed coordinates
Works on any site hosting the game (CrazyGames, MSN, etc.)
Requirements
Windows
64-bit Python 3.11 or 3.12 (the OCR dependency doesn't support 3.13+)
Setup
Extract this folder anywhere.
Run `START.bat`. It creates its own environment and installs dependencies on first run (internet needed once).
Usage
Open Space Waves in your browser.
Run `START.bat`.
When prompted, drag a box around just the game playfield — a tight selection keeps it running fast.
Click into the game, start/resume a level, then press F8 to start.
Press F9 to stop.
Useful flags:
```
START.bat --fast          # default: cheaper obstacle math, good for slower PCs
START.bat --no-fast       # exact (slower) obstacle math
START.bat --margin 1      # less safety buffer around obstacles (for very tight levels)
START.bat --title "MSN"   # if playing on a site whose tab title isn't matched by default
START.bat --preview       # show a debug overlay window
```
Notes
The bot pauses input whenever the game tab loses focus, and resumes automatically when it's focused again.
If you resize, zoom, or fullscreen the browser after selecting the playfield, restart and reselect.
Performance depends heavily on level difficulty; very tight sections may still be hard to clear reliably.
Tests
```
python -m unittest test_planner
```
